        example: "Consider a courtroom trial proceeding. The Creation Phase is the pre-trial docketing: the court clerk registers the names of all attorneys, witnesses, and scheduled exhibits into official court records before anyone speaks. The Execution Phase is the actual trial: attorneys step forward one by one to present arguments, cross-examine witnesses, and submit evidence in strict sequential order governed by parliamentary judicial procedure.",
