          "To understand the severity of this stall, consider what happens when a user swipes a finger on mobile: the hardware sends touch coordinates to the operating system, which delivers them to the browser compositor thread. If the compositor sees that an active DOM element falls inside an 'Input Event Handler Region' flagged with non-passive listeners, it cannot move the pixels on screen. It enqueues an event task onto the browser main thread task queue. If the main thread is blocked evaluating a complex component tree, 100 to 300 milliseconds of touch latency elapse before the scroll starts, creating a sluggish, broken user experience.",
