          "Frontend performance engineers diagnose this issue in Chrome DevTools using the Performance Panel. In the frame timeline, non-passive scroll handlers manifest as red bar markers indicating 'Dropped Frames' and long tasks exceeding the 50ms responsiveness threshold. To achieve zero-jank 120fps scrolling, the enterprise solution is to bypass React's synthetic event system entirely. By combining the useRef hook with native DOM lifecycle attachment in useEffect, engineers attach native listeners directly to the DOM node with the { passive: true } option flag (element.addEventListener('wheel', handleScroll, { passive: true })).",
